      "math_academy_id": "q-89720",
      "sequence_position": 17,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\ge 4).$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we have\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 4)=P(X>4).\n$$\n\nWe can perform this computation using the complement, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-(1-\\frac{{e}^{-4}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2{e}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
